  "id": "two-factor-analysis-of-variance",
  "term": "two-factor analysis of variance",
  "definition": "Two-factor analysis of variance is a statistical method used to test whether outcomes differ across two separate factors in the same study, such as magnification device and distance. It examines how each factor is related to the measured results when both are analyzed together.",
